49df6e12ef","position":{"commit_sha":"d973de86518eda50fe0821b0adce8ac807eef796","position":"1786099853270576001-f2593065-6561-4891-810b-3649df6e12ef"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-224_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"71441096-fe6a-495c-aef3-76e194ce469c","comments":[],"created_at":1785726328085394001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7a4a8aa9-e065-4583-96de-20190f640d86","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"12e4-8c74-a738-4014"}],"description":"Discovered by the sibling sweep while fixing 12e4 (a stalled snapshot fetch burned the full 300s `_GIT_TIMEOUT`).\n\n12e4 fixed the snapshot path: `_snapshot/git_fetch.fetch_origin` and `repo_snapshot._ensure_blobs_present` now pass `http.lowSpeedLimit`/`http.lowSpeedTime`, so a byte-starved transfer aborts on throughput in ~10s instead of at the wall-clock ceiling.\n\nThree other NETWORK git calls still carry a 300s wall-clock bound and no low-speed abort, so each has the identical exposure:\n\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py:367` (and the fetch at :401) — the review bot's own fetch of the Gerrit change, `_GIT_TIMEOUT = 300`. Closest sibling: same process, same per-review budget.\n- `src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py:107,124` — `fetch --quiet review|tickets`, `_GIT_TIMEOUT = 300`.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/init.py:398,419` — `_FETCH_TIMEOUT = 300`.\n\nDeliberately NOT in scope for 12e4: they are a different remote (self-hosted Gerrit) or a different command path, no stall has been measured on them, and folding them in would have widened an already-large change that was forced to split a module. The 30s callers (`_store/push.py`, `_store/sync.py`, `_store/event_append.py`, `_ref_lock.py`) are low value — 30s is already an order of magnitude tighter than the observed stall.\n\nReuse the seam 12e4 built: `rebar._snapshot.git_fetch.stall_abort_args()` and `is_stall_abort()` are module-public and take no snapshot-specific state, so each call site is a splice of `*stall_abort_args()` before the subcommand plus a decision about whether to retry.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each of the three 300s network fetch sites passes the low-speed options.\n- [ ] A test per site proves a zero-byte remote aborts as a stall, and that a dribbling remote is not aborted.\n- [ ] No new duplicate of the abort logic: the sites reuse `git_fetch.stall_abort_args()`.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f739caa2-8980-42d9-a7a7-7313543afb69","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"851e-19ef-31dd-4e38","ticket_type":"task","title":"Arm the throughput-keyed stall abort on the remaining 300s git fetches","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0326bb4a-e8ac-4400-b595-6d1e3c060c43","7a4a8aa9-e065-4583-96de-20190f640d86","961ec0f7-bba4-44a1-9aa5-d06115fa70bc","f739caa2-8980-42d9-a7a7-7313543afb69","f2593065-6561-4891-810b-3649df6e12ef"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786099853270576002,"uuid":"c37e7ae1-d661-4e5d-9fae-ead678c1d9b4"}